Maya Chen: Opening a micro-PR to clarify 429s/timeouts in the troubleshooting doc. Need a tiny JS snippet (respect Retry-After + fallback) and a 1-line migration note. @Arjun can you review?

Arjun Rao: Yep. Keep snippet under 10 lines and use client.text.generate. Mention 'context trim' once.

Maya Chen: Draft snippet:
```js
async function safeGen(client,prompt){
  try{return await client.text.generate({model:'redwood-1',prompt})}
  catch(e){
    if(e.status===429){await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r,parseInt(e.headers?.['Retry-After']||'1')*1000));return await client.text.generate({model:'redwood-1-small',prompt})}
    if(e.name==='TimeoutError')return await client.text.generate({model:'redwood-1-small',prompt})
    throw e
  }
}
```

Arjun Rao: Clean. Migration note: "Honor Retry-After; prefer backoff and canary rollouts; verify prefix caching to reduce tokens."

